    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d296">

                <pb facs="1073" n="923" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg923"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 7945/6–7.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                    Merry.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-09-20"><hi rendition="#italic">September 20,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 6.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 5, Nicaraguan Series, of the 29th ultimo, inclosing a copy of the
                    protest of the master of the Pacific Mail steamship <hi rendition="#italic">San
                        Juan</hi> against the searching of that vessel at Corinto by the Nicaraguan
                    authorities.</p>
                <p>In reply I inclose herewith, for your information, a copy of the department’s
                    instruction to the consul at Managua, in answer to his telegram reporting the
                    search of the vessel.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d296-a1.xml" xpointer="d296-a1"/>
            </div>
